      "translatedText": "Currently, the normal terrain output has a near\\-field elevation difference below 0\\.5 m and a far\\-field difference below 1 m; therefore, max_intensity = 2 m usually does not remove additional points; this does not mean the parameter was not read\\. If the input is changed, upstream is adjusted, or other marker points appear, the effect will change\\. The height and elevation difference thresholds use \"delete if less than the lower bound / greater than the upper bound,\" and boundary values pass\\.",
